            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "First change I'd like to see for this to merge.\n\nSecond change is where I think we should go in the future, not required for this patchset."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/intel-cpu/meson.build",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "should just be \n\nintel_cpu_inc += ['../../include']\n\nright?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/intel-cpu/meson.build",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "meson does not support what you are suggesting.\n\nIt may look retarded, but that's how it works i guess.\n\nFor meson the `include_directories` is a special object.\n\n```\n\n../src/intel-cpu/meson.build:4:22: ERROR: Object <[IncludeDirsHolder] holds [IncludeDirs]: <IncludeDirs src/['.']>> of type IncludeDirs does not support the `+` operator.\n\nA full log can be found at /home/alexander/upstreaming/dbus-sensors/build/meson-logs/meson-log.txt\nFAILED: build.ninja \n/usr/bin/meson --internal regenerate /home/alexander/upstreaming/dbus-sensors .\nninja: error: rebuilding 'build.ninja': subcommand failed\n[alexander@alexanderarchlinux dbus-sensors]$ git diff\ndiff --git a/src/intel-cpu/meson.build b/src/intel-cpu/meson.build\nindex bc05e4e..cd7697a 100644\n--- a/src/intel-cpu/meson.build\n+++ b/src/intel-cpu/meson.build\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n intel_cpu_inc = src_inc\n \n if not meson.get_compiler('cpp').has_header('linux/peci-ioctl.h')\n-    intel_cpu_inc = [src_inc, '../../include']\n+    intel_cpu_inc += ['../../include']\n endif\n \n executable(\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/meson.build",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Not needed on this patchset, but I would really like to see these files in these common includes encapsulated in at least a dependency declaration."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/meson.build",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Makes sense.\n\nWhat do you think of `src/common` to put the files which are used by multiple sensors?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/meson.build",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I have introduced `src/common` here https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/83895"
                }
            ],
